.TH CLEVO-CONTROL-TRAY 1 "" "clevo-control @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clevo\-control\-tray \- tray applet for the keyboard backlight of Clevo laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clevo\-control\-tray
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clevo\-control\-tray
shows an indicator in the system tray with a menu:
.TP
.B Choose color…
A color chooser. The chosen color is remembered, as with
.BR "clevoctl backlight color" .
.TP
Preset colors
White, red, orange, yellow, green, cyan, blue, purple, pink.
.TP
.B Brightness…
A window with a slider and the brightness as a percentage. It follows changes
made elsewhere, for example with the Fn keys.
.TP
.B Profile
The firmware performance profile, when the machine supports it.
.PP
The applet is started on login. Only one instance runs per session; starting
it again, for example from the application menu, opens the color chooser of
the running instance. While the keyboard backlight device is absent the
backlight entries are disabled, and they become usable when it appears.
.PP
On GNOME the indicator needs an AppIndicator extension, such as the
.B Ubuntu AppIndicators
extension enabled by default on Ubuntu.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when quit from the menu or when a running instance was activated, 1 if the
GTK or AppIndicator bindings are missing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/io.github.pavelnikanovich.ClevoControl.desktop
Autostart entry. Disable it in the desktop's startup applications settings, or
override it with a file of the same name in
.I ~/.config/autostart
containing
.BR Hidden=true .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clevoctl (1),
.BR clevo\-control (7)
